From: Xiaomi Mi MIX Linux port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_fg: report charging current as positive

The fuel gauge reports the current drawn from the battery, so current_now
was negative while charging. upower then reports a charging battery as
discharging. Invert it to the common convention: positive while charging,
negative while discharging.

---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
@@ -834,7 +834,14 @@
 		ret = chip->ops->get_capacity(chip, &val->intval);
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW:
+		/*
+		 * The FG reports the current drawn from the battery; userspace
+		 * (upower) expects positive while charging, negative while
+		 * discharging.
+		 */
 		ret = chip->ops->get_current(chip, &val->intval);
+		if (!ret)
+			val->intval = -val->intval;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW:
 		ret = chip->ops->get_voltage(chip, &val->intval);
